{
  "requirement": "The SDK exposes a tracked source read for domains supplying the source-node\nmapping under {cite}`requirements.sdk.sources.source_nodes`. It is available\nas the agent's `read_source` command.\n\nThe Rust interface has this shape; `SourceNodes` names the capability sketched\nin the source chapter:\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<'d, D: Domain + SourceNodes> InspectionContext<'d, D> {\n    /// Map this source address into the graph and read its node contents.\n    pub fn read_source(&self, item: &OutlineId) -> Result<D::NodeContent, D::Error>;\n}\n```",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "The requirement's structural obligation is a specific Rust interface. It is `impl<'d, D: Domain + SourceNodes> InspectionContext<'d, D> { pub fn read_source(&self, item: &OutlineId) -> Result<D::NodeContent, D::Error> }`. The `SourceNodes` capability is the application-supplied mapping from `OutlineId` to `NodeId`.\n\nI found no source that provides this interface:\n- A search of `crates` for `fn read_source` and `SourceNodes` returned nothing. There is no `SourceNodes` trait and no `read_source` method on `InspectionContext`.\n- `crates/habeas-sdk/src/graph.rs#impl[InspectionContext<'d, D>]` is bounded only by `D: Domain`. It exposes `read`, `read_snapshot` and `prepare_read`, and all three take a `D::NodeId`, not an `OutlineId`.\n- The two supplied implementation roots do not supply the signature either:\n  - `crates/habeas-sdk/src/agent/sources.rs#impl[SourceSession<…>/ToolSession<D>]/fn[definitions]` only builds the JSON tool definitions, including the `read_source` agent-command schema. This covers the \"available as the agent's `read_source` command\" sentence. It is not the Rust method.\n  - `crates/habeas-sdk/src/sources.rs#impl[SourceAnalysis<P>]/fn[parse]` only delegates to the provider's `parse`. It takes a `ResourceId` and returns a `ParsedSource`. It has no `OutlineId` parameter, no `Domain` or `SourceNodes` bound, and does not return `D::NodeContent`.\n- The tool dispatch in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/agent/sources.rs` takes a closure `F: Fn(&OutlineId, &ParsedSource) -> Result<Option<Dependency<…>>, String>`. It does not use a `SourceNodes` trait bound on the domain. Dispatch also carries separate requirements (`read_source.behavior` and `read_source.inputs`), so it is not the method this requirement specifies.\n\nThe required method on `InspectionContext` is therefore missing, and so is the `SourceNodes` bound it depends on. This is a structural gap. No {fixme} acknowledges it. I did not assess behavior or tests, since the structural obligation already fails.",
